  "term": "neuropeptide",
  "definition": "A neuropeptide is a naturally produced peptide that affects nervous system activity, either by acting directly at synapses or by changing how neural signals are regulated. It can be released by neurons as a neurotransmitter or by non-neuronal cells as a hormone.",
